  "definition": "Interferometric synthetic aperture radar (InSAR) compares the phase of two or more coregistered complex SAR observations of the same area. The phase difference records a change in the radar signal's travel path. With known acquisition geometry, this permits the construction of digital elevation models or the measurement of surface displacement between acquisitions.[^1]",
